{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-130083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={e}^{-2x}+x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-130083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{2}=1,{a}_{1}=2,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({e}^{-2x}+x) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})({e}^{-2x}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{-2x}+x)+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-2x}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{e}^{-2x}+1)+2(-2{e}^{-2x}+1) \\\\  & =4{e}^{-2x}-4{e}^{-2x}+2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-130083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6477498f472159f5747d570aac6faa791ca10b4dbb98a45ae4f566f3ce2a9d48"} {"question" "q-130083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Devel