 definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =(x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})-(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-79607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6477498f472159f5747d570aac6faa791ca10b4dbb98a45ae4f566f3ce2a9d48"} {"question" "q-79607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-79607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-79607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-337845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D=2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+4,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-337845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=2x,{f}_{1}=3,$ and ${f}_{0}=4.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =(2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+4)\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}})+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3/2}})+3(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3/2}})+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\frac{3}{4{x}^{5/2}}-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{3/2}}+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2{x}^{3/2}}-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{3/2}}+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dc