e apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={x}^{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({x}^{3}) & =x({x}^{3})\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({x}^{3})+{x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{x}^{2})+{x}^{3}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)+3{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\cdot 6+3{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & =6{x}^{4}+3{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}(3{x}^{2}+6x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-337986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6477498f472159f5747d570aac6faa791ca10b4dbb98a45ae4f566f3ce2a9d48"} {"question" "q-337986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-337986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{3}(3{x}^{2}+6x+2)"] ["math" "{x}^{3}(3{x}^{2}+6{x}^{2}+2x)"] ["math" "{x}^{3}(3{x}^{2}-6x+2)"] ["math" "{x}^{3}(3{x}^{2}-6x-2)"] ["math" "{x}^{3}(3{x}^{2}-6{x}^{2}+2x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-337986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}(3{x}^{2}+6x+2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-338254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $D(y)=xy\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+3y,$ then $D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-338254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=xy,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=0,$ and ${f}_{0}=3.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot (-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-338254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6477498f472159f5747d570aac6faa791ca10b4dbb98a45ae4f566f3ce2a9d48"} {"question" "q-338254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-338254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3+8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(6-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-3)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "q-338254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "446c24c9b2761f4e6db752c185f73e628109b555dcbadb7ba3ec2d7f367dbb3a"} {"question" "e-6570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D=\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}}+3 \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}+5,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=e^{- x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/example-6570.json" "file_sha256" "3ed4a497316367d92234ca742519c942ed787c800f7349ac831e3e0aeab33c6d"} {"question" "e-6570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = a_{2}\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + a_{1}\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + a_0y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  $a_2 = 1, a_1 = 3,$ and $a_0 = 5.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+5){e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{-x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{-x})+3\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/example-6570.json" "file_sha256" "3ed4a497316367d92234ca742519c942ed787c800f7349ac831e3e0aeab33c6d"} {"question" "e-6571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D=x^2\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}}{\\textrm d x^{3}}-5x \\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}} +9\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\ln{x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/example-6571.json" "file_sha256" "ce645281fc9c60208fab5c7c2507dee82c450a8ec5648d1fc53a2d9b1f9637f7"} {"question" "e-6571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} + f_{2}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x)y.\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = x^2, f_2 = -5x, f_1 = 9,$ and $f_0 = 0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x})-5x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})+9\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})-5x(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/example-6571.json" "file_sha256" "ce645281fc9c60208fab5c7c2507dee82c450a8ec5648d1fc53a2d9b1f9637f7"} {"question" "e-21785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $D(y)=y\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} - \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} + y^3,$ then calculate $D(e^{3x}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/example-21785.json" "file_sha256" "d33dca2d94e1edeaa154ba10eefe5b9e787725047388a70d2767f41dcec52604"} {"question" "e-21785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} +  f_{2}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = y,  f_2 = 0,  f_1 = -1,$ and $f_0 = y^2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y = e^{3x}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{x}) & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({e}^{3x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{3x})+{({e}^{3x})}^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & =27{e}^{6x}-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}({e}^{6x}+27{e}^{3x}-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/example-21785.json" "file_sha256" "d33dca2d94e1edeaa154ba10eefe5b9e787725047388a70d2767f41dcec52604"}] "usage" {"q-337559" [] "e-6570" [] "q-338253" [] "q-337986" [] "e-6571" [] "e-21785" []} "basis" 1278 "retractions" [[17592186078788 :question/problem "If $D(y) = y\\frac{d^{3}y}{dx^{3}} - xy\\frac{dy}{dx} + 2y$, then $D(\\sin x) =$"] [17592186078786 :question/problem "If $D(y) = y\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} - xy\\frac{dy}{dx} + 2y^{2}$, then $D(e^{2x}) =$"] [17592186078787 :question/problem "If $D(y) = xy\\frac{d^{3}y}{dx^{3}} + y\\frac{dy}{dx} + 2y$, then $D(x^{3}) =$"] [17592186078256 :question/problem "Given that $D=\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}}+3 \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}+5$, what is $D(y)$ for $y=e^{-x}$?"] [17592186078256 :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = a_{2}\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + a_{1}\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + a_0y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients\n\n$$\na_2 = 1, a_1 = 3\n$$\n\nand $a_0 = 5$.\n\nTo compute $D(y)$, we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD(y) &= D(e^{-x}) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}} + 3\\frac{d}{dx} + 5)e^{-x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}}(e^{-x}) + 3\\frac{d}{dx}(e^{-x}) + 5e^{-x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(-e^{-x}) + 3 \\cdot (-e^{-x}) + 5e^{-x} \\\\\n&= e^{-x} - 3e^{-x} + 5e^{-x} \\\\\n&= 3e^{-x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186078257 :question/problem "Given that $D=x^2\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}}{\\textrm d x^{3}}-5x \\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}} +9\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}$, what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\ln{x}$?"] [17592186078257 :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} + f_{2}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x)y\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nf_3 = x^2, f_2 = -5x, f_1 = 9\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nf_0 = 0\n$$\n\nTo compute $D(y)$, we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD(y) &= D(\\ln x) \\\\\n&= (x^{2}\\frac{d^{3}}{dx^{3}} - 5x\\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}} + 9\\frac{d}{dx})\\ln x \\\\\n&= x^{2}\\frac{d^{3}}{dx^{3}}(\\ln x) - 5x\\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}}(\\ln x) + 9\\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln x) \\\\\n&= x^{2}\\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x}) - 5x\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{1}{x}) + 9 \\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\\n&= x^{2}\\frac{d}{dx}(-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}) - 5x(-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}) + \\frac{9}{x} \\\\\n&= x^{2}(\\frac{2}{x^{3}}) + \\frac{5}{x} + \\frac{9}{x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{x} + \\frac{5}{x} + \\frac{9}{x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{16}{x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186078136 :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} - \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} + y^3$, then calculate $D(e^{3x})$."] [17592186078136 :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} + f_{2}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nf_3 = y, f_2 = 0, f_1 = -1\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nf_0 = y^2\n$$\n\nTo compute $D(y)$, we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function\n\n$$\ny = e^{3x}{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD(e^{x}) &= e^{3x}\\frac{d^{3}}{dx^{3}}(e^{3x}) - \\frac{d}{dx}(e^{3x}) + (e^{3x})^{3} \\\\\n&= e^{3x}\\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}}(3e^{3x}) - 3 \\cdot e^{3x} + e^{9x} \\\\\n&= e^{3x}\\frac{d}{dx}(9e^{3x}) - 3 \\cdot e^{3x} + e^{9x} \\\\\n&= 27e^{6x} - 3 \\cdot e^{3x} + e^{9x} \\\\\n&= e^{3x}(e^{6x} + 27e^{3x} - 3)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186075928 17592186075929 17592186075930 17592186075931 17592186075932 17592186075934 17592186075935 17592186075936 17592186075937 17592186075938 17592186075940 17592186075941 17592186075942 17592186075943 17592186075944] "immutable_fields" [[17592186075927 :answer-field/correct] [17592186075927 :answer-field/id] [17592186075927 :answer-field/key] [17592186075927 :answer-field/type] [17592186075933 :answer-field/correct] [17592186075933 :answer-field/id] [17592186075933 :answer-field/key] [17592186075933 :answer-field/type] [17592186075939 :answer-field/correct] [17592186075939 :answer-field/id] [17592186075939 :answer-field/key] [17592186075939 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
